From 26c5f8754c621746211809e4fcd07a69ac517722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:15:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] explorer: Add a Material 3 desktop style and make it
 the default.

The hand painted taskbar gets a Material 3 look next to the Luna one: a
flat bar with a launcher button, pill shaped task buttons and a two line
clock; a launcher sheet (user, built-in programs, start menu shortcuts,
places) instead of the start menu; and a background of large translucent
circles in place of the default wallpaper of the apps.

The colors are the tonal spot schemes of six seed colors, light and dark,
either following the window colors of the app or forced, picked in
Display Properties. Shapes are anti-aliased by computing the coverage of
each pixel. Roboto and Material Symbols (Apache 2.0) are resources of
explorer.exe, loaded with AddFontMemResourceEx.

HKCU\Software\Wine\Explorer\Taskbar: Style "material3" (default), "xp"
or "classic"; Accent 0-5; Mode 0 (follow the app), 1 (light), 2 (dark).
WINE_TASKBAR_STYLE overrides the style.

win32u draws the XP window frames with the xp style only, the Material 3
style keeps the plain Wine frames for now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
